<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lord of Mann</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lord of Mann is the title of the ruler of the Isle of Man. The Stanley family, granted the island in 1405, styled themselves Kings of Mann until 1504 and then Lords; the lordship passed to the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atholl">Atholl</a> in 1736, and its sovereign rights were sold to the British Crown in 1765. Since then the British monarch has held the title.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lord-of-mann.jpg" alt="Lord of Mann" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FXXX · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Isle_of_Man.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
